// Wire protocol for ifx-agent: a gRPC server (see agent/server_main.cpp)
// that wraps sqli::SqliConnection/SqliStatement directly (not the ODBC
// layer, to avoid a redundant translation step) so a Go host process (BOP's
// eventual Informix plugin) can drive this driver as a subprocess instead
// of linking it in-process. Chosen over a CGO shim or an existing Go ODBC
// package specifically so BOP survives a driver crash (subprocess boundary)
// and stays a pure-Go, C++-toolchain-free build (this driver ships as a
// separately-built, separately-distributed binary, e.g. pulled from a
// GitHub release, never vendored as source into BOP) - see STATUS.md's
// integration-mechanism section for the full rationale.
//
// Connect/Disconnect/ExecuteQuery (read-only) proved the mechanism end to
// end (process lifecycle, wire transport, sqli-layer wiring) first; a later
// revision added bind parameters and backup-faithful row reads (see
// Value's doc comment for the key design decision - a *shared* logical
// representation for both directions, not raw wire bytes). This revision
